  "text": " import math\n\ndef countPolynomials():\n    count = 0\n    for a in range(1, 100):  # Positive value for 'a'\n        if a == 0:\n            continue \n        for b in range(1, 100):  # Positive value for 'b'\n            if b == 0:\n                continue \n            roots = [3 - (b-a), 3, 3 + (b-a)]\n            \n            # Calculate coefficients\n            c1 = a * roots[0]\n            c2 = 3 * sum(roots) - 2 * a * roots[0]\n            c3 = roots[0] * roots[1] * roots[2]\n\n            # Check if 'a', 'b' and 'c1', 'c2', 'c3' are integers\n            if math.isclose(c1, round(c1)) and math.isclose(c2, round(c2)) and math.isclose(c3, round(c3)):\n                count += 1\n    return count\n  \ncount = countPolynomials()\nprint(count)",
